---
import LayerDiagram from '../components/LayerDiagram.astro';
import LickliderPortrait from '../components/LickliderPortrait.astro';
import { PUBLICATIONS } from '../data/publications';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// トップページはサイドメニューとページ内メニューを持たない。
// 本文は仮執筆 v0.1 の全文。省略せずドラフトのまま掲載する。英語化時に差し替える。
// (ドラフト末尾の「執筆メモ」はサイト非掲載の指定のため含めない)
const layers = [
  {
    n: 'Layer 1',
    title: 'nomue Record (open specification) and verifier',
    body: 'An open format that records how each research output — figures, Legend, Methods, Results, Claim — was generated from its input data, declarations, statistical rules, and computations. A Record binds each approved output to its underlying evidence in machine-readable form, making the basis of approval independently verifiable. The accompanying open-source verifier lets third parties check the Record’s internal consistency without depending on our software. Neither the Record nor its verification requires trust in us — a necessary condition for this layer to serve as a foundation for accountability.',
  },
  {
    n: 'Layer 2',
    title: 'nomue (application)',
    body: 'An execution environment that generates and maintains research outputs with the Record as their canonical source. From research data and research intent, it produces analyses, figures, Legend, Methods, Results, and Claim on the same underlying evidence. Humans approve each output with its evidence attached. When data, declarations, or analyses change, the outputs and approvals they affect are invalidated, requiring regeneration and re-approval.',
  },
];

const latest = [...PUBLICATIONS].sort((a, b) => b.sortKey.localeCompare(a.sortKey));
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Agenda</p>
      <h1>Engineering Accountability<br />at Machine Scale</h1>
      <div class="lede">
        <p>
          AI has scaled generation.<br />
          What must scale next is approval.
        </p>
        <p>Licklider builds the engineering foundation for responsible approval.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="cta">
        <a href="https://github.com/licklider-ai/nomue-verifier" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          nomue verifier →
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="sections">
    <section class="band band--single">
      <div class="band-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">Thesis</p>
        <div class="band-body">
        <p>
          AI now generates intellectual work — analyses, figures, prose, code — far beyond the pace at which humans can produce it. The institutions of verification and approval, designed for an era when generation was scarce, have not kept up. When the volume of output exceeds human capacity to verify it, the rate-limiting step shifts from generation to approval.
        </p>
        <p>
          When approval becomes the bottleneck, it turns into a formality. People sign off on work whose basis they cannot fully verify, and those signatures gradually lose their power to establish responsibility when something goes wrong. Accountability comes not from a signature but from a connection to verifiable evidence. Approval severed from that evidence does not transfer responsibility; it hollows it out.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not trying to automate responsibility itself. We are trying to engineer the conditions under which responsibility has substance. We call this engineering accountability. Just as software engineering shifted part of the burden of correctness from human attention to mechanical verification — type checking, continuous integration, audit logs — the intellectual work AI generates needs a layer that mechanically maintains the consistency between outputs and their evidence, and that third parties can verify independently.
        </p>
        <p>
          Licklider starts building this layer in scientific research. Science asks not only who is responsible for a claim, but which data, analyses, and judgments that claim rests on. The connection between claim and evidence is a condition for the work to count at all. What holds up in that environment can, in time, extend to regulation, auditing, medicine, finance, and any decision-making that involves AI.
        </p>
        <p>
          What the AI era needs is not just layers for generating more. It needs a layer that lets humans take responsibility for what has been generated.
        </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="what-we-build" class="band band--single">
      <div class="band-inner band-inner--wide">
        <p class="eyebrow">What We Build</p>
        <LayerDiagram layers={layers} />

        <div class="band-body">
          <p class="lead">
            We place the basis of trust not in generated outputs but in a verifiable record. Generation is a layer of convenience; the record and its verification are the substance.
          </p>

          <p class="more">
            <a href="https://github.com/licklider-ai/nomue-verifier" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">→ nomue verifier</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band band--single">
      <div class="band-inner band-inner--wide">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why "Licklider"</p>
        <div class="why">
          <div class="band-body">
            <p>
              In "Man-Computer Symbiosis" (1960), J. C. R. Licklider clearly articulated a division of labor in which humans set goals and exercise judgment while computers carry out the routine work.
            </p>
            <p>
              In the decades since, generation has moved to the machine's side, while approval and responsibility have stayed with humans. We believe this new division of labor needs a new foundation.
            </p>
            <p>Our name refers to the original blueprint for that division of labor.</p>
          </div>
          <LickliderPortrait />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="latest" class="band">
      <p class="eyebrow">Latest</p>
      <div class="band-body">
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table>
            <tbody>
              {
                latest.map((row) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td class="latest-date">{row.date}</td>
                    <td>
                      <a href={row.href}>{row.title}</a>
                    </td>
                    <td class="latest-category">
                      <a href={`/${row.category.toLowerCase()}/`}>{row.category}</a>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-faint);
  }

  .hero-inner {
    max-width: var(--shell);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 7rem var(--gutter) 6rem;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.25rem);
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    color: var(--ink-1);
  }

  .cta {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .cta a {
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
    padding-bottom: 3px;
  }

  .cta a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .sections {
    max-width: var(--shell);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--gutter);
  }

  .band {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 4rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-faint);
  }

  .band:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .band > .eyebrow {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
  }

  .band-body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  /* 1 ペインの段。見出しを本文の上に置き、内容ごと中央に寄せる。
     幅は 2 ペイン時の本文列と同じに保つ */
  .band--single {
    display: block;
  }

  .band-inner {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* 図の段は、2 ペイン時の 2 列目 (シェル 71rem − 見出し 12rem − 間隔 3rem) と同じ幅 */
  .band-inner--wide {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }

  .band-inner > .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .band-inner--wide .band-body {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  /* Why "Licklider": 左に本文、右に人物画。人物画は本文の高さに合わせて中央へ */
  .why {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 16rem);
    gap: 3.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .why .band-body {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .band-body > :last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  strong {
    font-weight: 400;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .more {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  /* Latest: 3 分類を混在表示するため、各行に分類ラベルを置く */
  .latest-date {
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .latest-category {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    text-align: right;
  }

  .latest-category a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  tbody tr:first-child td {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-faint);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .hero-inner {
      padding: 4rem var(--gutter) 3.5rem;
    }

    .band {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 1.25rem;
      padding: 3rem 0;
    }

    /* 人物画は本文の下へ回して中央に置く */
    .why {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2.5rem;
    }

    .why :global(.portrait) {
      max-width: 15rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
  }
</style>
